<p class="text-white/70">Yes, B2B companies particularly benefit from AEO's authority-building approach, which accelerates trust development in complex buying processes and provides more efficient customer acquisition than traditional keyword-focused SEO strategies.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What are the main risk differences between SEO and AEO ROI?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Traditional SEO carries high algorithmic risk where single updates can eliminate years of investment. AEO distributes risk across multiple AI platforms and builds more defensible authority positioning that's harder for competitors to displace.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">Can companies implement both SEO and AEO simultaneously?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Yes, many companies maintain traditional SEO while implementing AEO strategies. However, resource allocation typically shifts toward AEO over time as AI search adoption accelerates and ROI advantages become more pronounced.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">How do you measure AEO ROI differently than traditional SEO ROI?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">AEO ROI measurement focuses on answer authority metrics, AI search visibility, and conversion quality rather than traditional traffic volume and keyword rankings. This creates clearer attribution and more actionable optimization insights.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What is the typical payback period for AEO compared to traditional SEO?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Traditional SEO typically shows positive ROI after 8-10 months, while AEO can demonstrate value within 4-6 months due to lower competition in AI engines. However, the absolute traffic volume from traditional SEO remains higher in the short term.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">How do conversion rates compare between traditional SEO and AEO traffic?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">AEO traffic often shows higher conversion rates because AI engines provide more contextual, decision-stage responses. Users arriving from AI-powered search results are typically further along in their buyer journey compared to traditional organic search visitors.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What percentage of budget should be allocated to AEO versus traditional SEO?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">A balanced approach typically allocates 70% to traditional SEO for immediate results and 30% to AEO for future positioning. Organizations in competitive markets may start with 80/20 allocation, while early adopters in emerging industries might reverse this ratio.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">Can AEO completely replace traditional SEO investment?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">No, AEO cannot completely replace traditional SEO in the current market. Traditional SEO still drives the majority of organic search traffic. AEO should be viewed as a complementary strategy that prepares for the future of search while traditional SEO maintains current performance.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What metrics best measure AEO ROI compared to traditional SEO ROI?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Traditional SEO ROI focuses on organic traffic growth, keyword rankings, and conversion improvements. AEO ROI should be measured through AI engine visibility, brand mention accuracy, decision-stage traffic capture, and competitive positioning in AI responses. Both require different KPI frameworks for accurate assessment.</p>
</div>
